     I*
     I* RPG/400 input specifications: record identification codes, field
     I* descriptions, data structures, subfields and named constants.
     I*
     I* Member: RPGINP   Compilable: no (declarations only, no cycle)
     I* Source: RPG/400 Reference SC09-1817, chapter 8 (Tables 21-29)
     I*         and chapter 3 (indicator rules).
     I* Retrieved: 2026-07-26
     I*
     I* Record identification: 7-14 file  14-16 AND/OR  15-16 sequence
     I* 17 number  18 option  19-20 record identifying indicator
     I* 21-27, 28-34, 35-41 record identification codes
     I* Field description: 43 format  44-47 from  48-51 to  52 decimals
     I* 53-58 name  59-60 control  61-62 match  63-64 relation
     I* 65-70 field indicators (plus, minus, zero or blank)
     I* 75-80 comments, shown here in lower case
     I*  1         2         3         4         5         6         7         8
     I*8901234567890123456789012345678901234567890123456789012345678901234567890
     I*
     I* Program described file. A record identification code is a
     I* position, an optional N, C/Z/D, and the character to match.
     IORDHDR  AA1 01   1 CH
     I       OR   02   1 CD
     I       AND       2NCX
     I            03   1 CT   2 Z9  80ND*                                 trlr
     I*
     I* Sequence checking uses two digits in 15-16 and 1 or N in 17.
     IPAYTRN  011O10   1 CA
     I        02NO11   1 CB
     I*
     I* Record identifying indicators may be 01-99, H1-H9, L1-L9,
     I* LR, U1-U8 or RT. Look-ahead uses ** in 19-20.
     ICTLFILE     L1   1 C1
     I            H1   1 C2
     I            LR   1 C9
     I            U1   1 CU
     I            RT   1 CR
     I            **   1 CL                                               lookah
     I*
     I* The identifying character in 27 may be a blank, as in
     I* position 1 is not blank. Storing source as a text file
     I* strips it, so the entry ends at position 26.
     IINVHDR  NS  01   1NC
     I        NS  02   1 C
     I*
     I* Field descriptions. Position 43 gives the internal format:
     I* blank zoned, P packed, B binary, L and R signed left or right.
     I                                        1   6 ORDNBRL1              key
     I                                        7  26 CUSTNM
     I                                    P  27  312ORDAMT      202122
     I                                    B  32  350ORDQTY    01
     I                                    L  36  422DISCNT        30
     I                                    R  43  492FRIGHT
     I                                       50  55 ORDDAT  M1
     I                                       56  61 SHPDAT  M2MR
     I                                       62  62 STATUS    RT    99
     I*
     I* Externally described file: only the record format name in
     I* 7-14, and renamed fields in 21-30 with the program name in
     I* 53-58.
     ICUSTREC     20
     I              CUSTOMERNAME                    CUSTNM
     I              CUSTOMERBAL                     CUSTBLL2    404142
     I*
     I* Data structures. Position 17 E means externally described,
     I* 18 is I initialize, S program status, or U data area.
     IORDDS       DS                             64                       order
     I                                        1   6 DSORD
     I                                        7  26 DSCUST
     I                                    P  27  312DSAMT
     IINITDS     IDS                             20
     I I            'PENDING'                 1  10 DSSTAT
     I I            0                        11  200DSCNT
     IMULTDS      DS                         12  30                       occurs
     I                                        1  10 MDNAME
     I                                    P  11  152MDAMT
     IEXTDS     E DSCUSTMAST                                              extds
     I              CUSTOMERNAME                    EXNAME
     IPSDS       SDS                                                      status
     I                                        1  10 PSPGM
     I                                      254 263 PSSTAT
     ILDADS      UDS                            256                       lda
     I                                        1  10 LDACO
     I*
     I* Named constants: the literal in 21-42, C in 43, name in
     I* 53-58. A constant continues on the next line when a hyphen
     I* is coded in place of the closing quote. On such a line the
     I* literal has no closing quote, so it runs to the end of the
     I* line and takes the C in 43 and the name in 53-58 with it.
     I              'PAYROLL SYSTEM'      C         TITLE
     I              12                    C         MAXTRY
     I              3.14159               C         PI
     I              X'FF'                 C         HIBYTE
     I              *BLANKS               C         EMPTY
     I              'ABCDEF-              C         CHARCN
     I              'GHIJK'
     I              -4096                 C         NEGCN
     I              123456-               C         NUMCN
     I              789
     I              X'0102-               C         HEXCN
     I              '0304'
     I*
     I* A page and line number in 1-5 does not disturb the columns.
05010I                                        1  10 SEQFLD                seq
